## Why This Is Asked

Real-world CNPA stacks face subtle, cross-component bottlenecks during feature flag rollouts. Isolating whether latency comes from cache invalidation, the indexing pipeline, or rollout logic is critical for safe canary deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Outbox pattern and atomic writes across DB and messaging
- Idempotent indexing/upserts in Elasticsearch
- Cache invalidation correctness and TTL strategies
- End-to-end tracing across HTTP, DB, Kafka, Redis, ES
- Canary deployments and feature flag rollout risk controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: idempotent index update for Elasticsearch
async function upsertIndex(docId, doc) {
  // upsert via Elasticsearch; idempotent on duplicates
  await es.update({
    index: 'pricing',
    id: docId,
    body: { doc, doc_as_upsert: true }
  });
}
```

